comments.body:
@New Amsterdammer - Sorry that your Mom also died from lung cancer.  Thanks for your thoughtful post.

@Kathy - Thanks so much Kathy!!!

@Paul Klenk - Thanks Paul.  When I was in junior high, I would walk to our town's public library and "read" The New Yorker.  I understood a lot of the stories but what I was really interested in was the advertising because that told me a lot about New York and New Yorkers. Eventually I became more engrossed with the articles than I did with the ads.  But that was really how I first became familiar with anything regarding New York, especially NYC!
